# What DirectAdmin 1.709 writes when the backup task asks for a chosen
# set of data rather than all of it. Taken from the disposable account
# gzv0908a on the validation host on 2026-09-09; the domain is under
# .invalid and there is no customer data here.
#
# The task line is the one the admin backup page posts:
#
#   action=backup&owner=admin&type=admin&value=multiple&when=now
#   &where=local&local_path=<dir>&select0=<user>
#   &what=select&option0=<value>&option1=<value>...
#
# run through "directadmin taskq --run=", and the option values are the
# ones the page's fourth step offers: domain, subdomain, email,
# email_data, emailsettings, forwarder, autoresponder, vacation, list,
# ftp, ftpsettings, database, database_data, trash.
#
# Leaving out "domain" takes with it both domains/ and the nested
# backup/home.tar.zst -- the whole of the account's own files. What is
# left is what Gniza cannot read from /home itself.
#
# Leaving out "email" as well takes imap/, but it also takes the
# mailboxes' own passwords (backup/<domain>/email/passwd), their quotas
# and their webmail settings, which are not in /home either. So "email"
# stays, and imap/ is dropped from the metadata part after unpacking
# instead: the messages are read from /home/<user>/imap in place.

## what=select, every option except domain
backup/
backup/gzv0908a.gniza-test.invalid/
backup/gzv0908a.gniza-test.invalid/email/
backup/gzv0908a.gniza-test.invalid/email/passwd
backup/gzv0908a.gniza-test.invalid/email/data/
backup/gzv0908a.gniza-test.invalid/email/data/webmail/
